452 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Client Responsibilities\n\nThe client is responsible for\072\n Paying hosting invoices by their due date\n Keeping billing and contact details current\n Maintaining and renewing the website domain\n Keeping CMS and account access secure\n Ensuring website content is accurate and lawful\n Maintaining any required privacy policy\054 consent wording or legal notices\n Paying for external services or subscriptions connected to the website\n\nUnless agreed separately\054 CB Works is not responsible for the client\031s domain registration\054 business email\054 internal IT systems or use of information collected through website forms\056\n\nBackups \046 Recovery\n\nNetlify\054 DatoCMS and other platforms may maintain their own system backups\056 These should not be treated as a permanent or guaranteed archive\056\n\nCB Works does not guarantee that deleted or overwritten content can always be recovered\056 Where possible\054 CB Works may assist with recovery\054 although additional work may be quoted separately\056\n\nThe client should retain copies of important content\054 images and business records outside the CMS\056\n\nPayments \046 Suspension\n\nHosting is billed monthly or annually from the website launch date or another agreed start date\056\n\nIf payment becomes overdue\054 CB Works will contact the client and provide an opportunity to resolve the issue\056\n\nIf payment remains outstanding for more than 14 days after written notice\054 CB Works may pause the website and related services until all outstanding amounts have been paid\056\n\nCB Works is not responsible for downtime or business loss caused by hosting being paused due to unpaid invoices\056\n\nCancellation \046 Handover\n\nThe client may cancel hosting by providing 30 days\031 written notice\056 Monthly hosting will continue during the notice period\054 and annual hosting payments are generally not refundable\056\n\nAll outstanding invoices must be paid before the website is transferred\056\n\nTo move the website away from CB Works hosting\054 the client will need to create\072\n A Netlify account\n A DatoCMS account\n\nThe client must provide CB Works with access to these accounts so the website hosting\054 CMS and code repository can be transferred where supported by the platforms\056\n\nUp to one hour of standard transfer assistance is included\056 Additional migration work\054 DNS changes\054 troubleshooting or redevelopment will be quoted separately\056\nOnce transferred\054 the client becomes responsible for all hosting costs\054 security\054 maintenance\054 platform updates\054 account access and technical support\056\n\nChanges to the Service\n\nCB Works may update its hosting packages\054 inclusions or pricing to reflect changes in platform costs\054 exchange rates\054 website usage or the level of support required\056\n\nAt least 30 days\031 notice will be provided before a material pricing change takes effect\056 The client may cancel the hosting service before the new price begins\056\n\nCB Works may also pause or end the service where the website presents an urgent security or legal risk\054 is used for unlawful activity or the client seriously breaches these terms\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 453 0 R
     /Pg 444 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
